  {
   "id": "deployment",
   "title": "The Greeks close the Hot Gates",
   "time": "Day 0 to 4",
   "narrative": "Xerxes brought his host down from Thessaly and halted before the narrow coastal pass of Thermopylae. King Leonidas of Sparta had marched north with his 300 Spartans and a mixed force of allied Greeks, perhaps 7,000 men in all by the modern standard count. He posted them at the middle gate, where the Phocians had once built a wall, and where the cliffs of Mt Kallidromos on one side and the Malian Gulf on the other left a passage of roughly 100 metres. The Persians camped in the plain to the west and for four days did nothing, waiting for the Greeks to give way.",
