   "id": "archers",
   "title": "Day one: the arrow barrage",
   "time": "Day 5, morning",
   "narrative": "On the fifth day Xerxes finally ordered an attack. He opened with 5,000 archers, who shot from beyond the reach of the Greek spears. The volleys did little harm: bronze helmets and big wooden shields caught most of the arrows, and the defenders stood behind their wall where the pass was narrowest, so few of them were exposed at any time. The Persians had to send in men on foot.",
