   "id": "medes",
   "title": "Day one: Medes and Cissians",
   "time": "Day 5, midday",
   "narrative": "Xerxes sent 10,000 Medes and Cissians to take the defenders alive. They attacked in waves against the Greek front. Their shields were lighter and their spears and swords shorter than those of the hoplites, and in the narrow ground they could not use their numbers. Herodotus says the Greeks fought by city contingents and rotated men to rest, and that Xerxes leapt up three times from his throne as his troops were cut down. Ctesias claims the first wave was slaughtered for the loss of two or three Spartans.",
