   "time": "Day 5, afternoon",
   "narrative": "The same day the king committed his best troops, the 10,000 Immortals. They fared no better than the Medes. The Greeks are said to have used a trick, turning as if in flight and then wheeling on the pursuers once they had broken their own order. Whatever the details, the Persians could not make the weight of their numbers count in a space only one hundred metres wide, and withdrew at dusk.",
