  {
   "id": "council",
   "title": "Leonidas dismisses most of the army",
   "time": "Dawn, day 7",
   "narrative": "Warned that he was surrounded, Leonidas held a council. Some wished to retreat; he himself would not leave, and told the allies that they were free to go. Most did, or were ordered away. Retreating over the open ground beyond the pass would have exposed them to cavalry, so the rearguard gave the rest a chance to get clear. Herodotus is unsure whether they left on orders or of their own accord. The 300 Spartans stayed, with 700 Thespians under Demophilus and about 400 Thebans.",
