   "id": "sally",
   "title": "The Greeks sally out",
   "time": "Morning, day 7",
   "narrative": "Xerxes poured libations at sunrise and waited until the Immortals could be expected to have come down the mountain, then ordered his front to advance. Knowing that they were about to be caught from behind, the Greeks left their wall and went out into the wider part of the pass to kill as many of the enemy as they could. They fought with spears until the shafts broke and then with their short swords. Two brothers of Xerxes, Abrocomes and Hyperanthes, fell. Leonidas was killed by arrows, and the Greeks won the fight over his body.",
