  {
   "id": "hill",
   "title": "Withdrawal to Kolonos Hill",
   "time": "Midday, day 7",
   "narrative": "Hydarnes' column came out of the hills onto the road behind the defenders and the Immortals pressed in from the front. The Greeks drew back through the wall onto a mound. The Thebans broke away, held up their hands and surrendered, though some were killed first, and Xerxes later had the survivors branded. Marinatos' 1939 excavation found masses of Persian arrowheads on Kolonos Hill, which is why the final stand is now placed there and not on a lower rise by the wall.",
