   "title": "The pass is open",
   "time": "Evening, day 7",
   "narrative": "The way to Phocis, Boeotia and Attica now lay open to the Persian army. The defenders had delayed it for several days, and the Greek fleet at Artemisium withdrew after hearing the news. The 300 Spartans and the Thespians were wiped out, while some 3,000 men of the other contingents had got away to fight again. Xerxes advanced south; the Greeks would answer at Salamis and Plataea.",
